{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788129499440,"sessionID":"ses_fab2d85e2ffebDq1A7tlFaR4vv","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-b5aa487d01388fce","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"Q35","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/plans/questions.md"},"output":"Found 6 matches\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/plans/streams.md:\n  Line 88: a non-star pattern); Q35 (what stdout is -- the sink rule deliberately avoids answering);\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/plans/questions.md:\n  Line 55: | [Q35](#q35-what-are-stdout-and-stderr-and-does-a-program-write-or-return) | What are stdout and stderr, and does a program write or return? | OPEN; `jsonlines` is now a top-level-only sink with no result type, which removes a placeholder answer without deciding the question |\n\n  Line 480: ### Q35. What are stdout and stderr, and does a program write or return?\n\n  Line 541:   ([Q35](#q35-what-are-stdout-and-stderr-and-does-a-program-write-or-return)), which makes\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/plans/language-oddities.md:\n  Line 353: and deliberate (a sink's result cannot be observed, so it has none, and Q35 stays open); the\n\n  Line 360: avoid prejudging Q35 (what stdout is), which the current design carefully does not.\n","metadata":{"matches":6,"truncated":false},"title":"Q35","time":{"start":1788129499432,"end":1788129499439}},"id":"prt_054d2c57f001odWp1dkq2CbAbb","sessionID":"ses_fab2d85e2ffebDq1A7tlFaR4vv","messageID":"msg_054d2b92c001vuEIgAMr9VM7km"}}
