{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788129519819,"sessionID":"ses_fab2d85e2ffebDq1A7tlFaR4vv","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-955890c210e7bbe9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/plans/board.yaml"},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/plans/board.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # The task board (scheduler v2, maintainer-specified 2026-08-29): every unblocked task is by\n2: # definition ready to be picked up, and up to EIGHT build lanes run at once\n3: # (raised from five 2026-08-30; decide rows queue for the maintainer separately\n4: # and never consume a lane or a ready-set slot).\n5: #\n6: # Done rows do not live here (issue #113): landing a task MOVES its row to\n7: # plans/board-archive.yaml (same schema, append-only) instead of flipping status in place, so\n8: # this file stays the ~quarter of the board that is still live -- the loop's single most-read\n9: # file, and every tick pays for its length. A needs/soft id not found on this live board is\n10: # satisfied: it must have landed and been archived. Consult the archive only for provenance,\n11: # never to decide whether something is blocking.\n12: #\n13: # Fields: id (slug; gh:N when a GitHub issue carries the spec), title, kind, needs, soft,\n14: # prio, status.\n15: #   kind: build  = delegatable implementation work (enwiro-delegate out, land-delegated-work in)\n16: #         decide = needs a grilling/design session with the maintainer before anything builds\n17: #   needs: HARD blockers -- forced order; a task with an un-done need is not pickable at all.\n18: #          An id absent from this file is satisfied, not missing.\n19: #   soft:  SOFT blockers -- convenient order that saves effort or time (file-footprint\n20: #          overlaps, avoid-rework sequencing). A task with un-done soft blockers is still\n21: #          pickable, just ranked below less-soft-blocked work. Same absent-is-satisfied rule.\n22: #   prio:  1 (highest) .. 5; omitted means 3. Sorts WITHIN a soft-blockedness category, so\n23: #          soft order outweighs raw priority -- but among fully unblocked tasks, prio alone\n24: #          decides. Efficiency/process improvements are prio tasks by standing rule.\n25: #   status: todo | delegated  (done rows move to board-archive.yaml; \"blocked\" is derived from\n26: #           needs, never stored)\n27: #   lane:  which worker-pool lane a delegated row runs in (lane-1 .. lane-5, gh:124); the\n28: #          tick scripts resolve its worktree through the env symlink. Absent means the\n29: #          classic per-issue env (worktree issue-<N>). Set at dispatch, travels to the\n30: #          archive with the row.\n31: #   model: which model the delegated session runs -- omitted means sonnet (the default for\n32: #          regular build work); \"fable\" is reserved for design-heavy or cross-cutting builds\n33: #          the coordinator judges worth it; \"haiku\" is for mechanical work with an obvious\n34: #          done-state (renames, sweeps, small config/UI tweaks) where cheaper and faster\n35: #          beats smarter (maintainer rule, 2026-08-30). decide rows have no model; they are\n36: #          the human.\n37: #\n38: # Picking the ready set (drive skill executes this): drop hard-blocked rows (done rows are\n39: # already gone); group the rest by soft-blockedness (count of un-done soft blockers, in-flight\n40: # ones included); least soft-blocked category first, prio within each. TWO queues from that\n41: # ordering (2026-08-30): every ready decide goes to the maintainer's grill/mail queue, and the\n42: # top ready builds fill the free lanes up to the cap. List position is a tiebreak only. A\n43: # needs-cycle, or todo rows remaining with nothing pickable and nothing in flight, is a\n44: # deadlock and gets reported.\n45: - id: local-binding-design\n46:   issue: gh:87\n47:   title: Grill local bindings inside an expression -- the where/as shaped gap (emuto survey adopt)\n48:   kind: decide\n49:   needs: []\n50:   status: todo\n51: \n52: - id: csv-inputs-idea\n53:   issue: gh:88\n54:   title: Grill the DSV source shape -- delimiter vs nullary sources (worker analysis, gh:88 comment)\n55:   kind: decide\n56:   needs: []\n57:   prio: 4\n58:   status: todo\n59: \n60: - id: int64-wire-form\n61:   issue: gh:89\n62:   title: Decide the Int64 wire form -- input refuses it pending the codec call (gh:83 escalation)\n63:   kind: decide\n64:   needs: []\n65:   prio: 3\n66:   status: todo\n67: \n68: - id: euler-slow-fragments-2\n69:   issue: gh:93\n70:   title: Batch 3's correct-but-slow problems, parked with the same tier question as gh:90\n71:   kind: decide\n72:   needs: []\n73:   soft: [euler-slow-fragments]\n74:   prio: 3\n75:   status: todo\n76: \n77: - id: python-recursion-limit\n78:   issue: gh:132\n79:   title: Python backend never raises sys' default recursion limit -- breaks real-sized recursive programs (found via euler-11)\n80:   kind: build\n81:   needs: []\n82:   prio: 3\n83:   status: delegated\n84: \n85: - id: euler-pages-restore\n86:   issue: gh:133\n87:   title: Restore the Euler 8/11/13/18 docs pages now that tests/euler_real_data.rs verifies them (gh:129 follow-up)\n88:   kind: build\n89:   needs: []\n90:   soft: [python-recursion-limit]\n91:   prio: 3\n92:   status: delegated\n93: \n94: - id: projection-style-demotion\n95:   issue: gh:99\n96:   title: Demote map(.field) for pure projection -- style and sweep, not a refusal\n97:   kind: build\n98:   needs: []\n99:   prio: 3\n100:   soft: [concat-retirement]\n101:   status: delegated\n102: \n103: - id: euler-slow-fragments\n104:   issue: gh:90\n105:   title: Decide the slow-fragment tier -- Euler 10 and 14 solve correctly but cost minutes on the weak backends\n106:   kind: decide\n107:   needs: []\n108:   prio: 3\n109:   status: todo\n110: \n111: - id: matcher-totality-and-alt-design\n112:   title: Grill matcher totality measurement, alt-composition (one arm, many patterns), and the parser-combinator stress test\n113:   kind: decide\n114:   needs: [auto-matchers-design]\n115:   prio: 1\n116:   status: todo\n117: \n118: - id: matcher-model-clarification\n119:   issue: gh:122\n120:   title: Grill the matching system's conceptual model -- base matcher kinds, how conditions enter, composition with type matchers (maintainer compose note)\n121:   kind: decide\n122:   needs: []\n123:   soft: [matcher-totality-and-alt-design]\n124:   prio: 2\n125:   status: todo\n126: \n127: - id: variant-types-flip\n128:   title: Variants become capitalized types with lowercase constructors, per the auto-matchers ratification -- subtype rules planned first, then the migration (corpus, examples, README, and docs/guides+tutorial+reference)\n129:   kind: build\n130:   needs: [matcher-totality-and-alt-design]\n131:   prio: 2\n132:   model: fable\n133:   status: todo\n134: \n135: - id: shell-out-design\n136:   title: Grill the syntax for calling external CLI programs -- bash-convenient or better\n137:   kind: decide\n138:   needs: []\n139:   status: todo\n140: \n141: - id: stdin-syntax-design\n142:   title: Grill the one-stdin-source syntax, once type flow makes parse steps possible\n143:   kind: decide\n144:   needs: [type-flow-rework]\n145:   status: todo\n146: \n147: - id: stdin-redesign-build\n148:   title: Retire the three stdin keywords for the one-source design\n149:   kind: build\n150:   needs: [stdin-syntax-design]\n151:   model: fable\n152:   status: todo\n153: \n154: - id: function-signature-ergonomics\n155:   title: Grill destructuring params and pipeline-first bodies -- wizard round with real code\n156:   kind: decide\n157:   needs: []\n158:   status: todo\n159: \n160: - id: overloading-and-traits-design\n161:   title: Grill function overloading and Rust-style traits -- the direction that dissolves concat and kin\n162:   kind: decide\n163:   needs: [precedent-survey]\n164:   status: todo\n165: \n166: - id: mutation-semantics-design\n167:   title: Grill privileged/shared references -- mutation as a static optimization, no borrow checker\n168:   kind: decide\n169:   needs: []\n170:   prio: 4\n171:   status: todo\n172: \n173: - id: void-functions-design\n174:   issue: gh:58\n175:   title: Grill void functions -- formalize functions that map to nothing but may have side effects (maintainer idea, streams tutorial annotation)\n176:   kind: decide\n177:   needs: []\n178:   status: todo\n179: \n180: - id: range-stream-source-design\n181:   issue: gh:127\n182:   title: Grill whether range should become a Stream source -- Q1/Q13 amendment to ADR 0001 (prelude-inventory approved finding, gh:105/gh:121)\n183:   kind: decide\n184:   needs: []\n185:   status: todo\n186: \n187: - id: q37-float-semantics\n188:   title: Grill Q37 -- float printing agreement, NaN/Infinity, division by zero\n189:   kind: decide\n190:   needs: []\n191:   status: todo\n192: \n193: - id: benchmark-goals\n194:   title: Grill what workloads define the performance thesis, then plan the benchmark suite\n195:   kind: decide\n196:   needs: []\n197:   prio: 4\n198:   status: todo\n199: \n200: - id: float-build\n201:   title: Implement Float (IEEE binary64 per ADR 0007) across the backends\n202:   kind: build\n203:   needs: [q37-float-semantics]\n204:   status: todo\n205: \n206: - id: lines-utf8-edge\n207:   issue: gh:102\n208:   title: Pin what a non-UTF-8 byte arriving via lines does, on every backend\n209:   kind: decide\n210:   needs: []\n211:   status: todo\n212: \n213: - id: jq-printer-cycle-refusal\n214:   issue: gh:116\n215:   title: jq -- recursive-enum printers refuse a mutual cycle the way ordered() refuses one (issue-94 review)\n216:   kind: build\n217:   needs: []\n218:   prio: 3\n219:   soft: [concat-retirement]\n220:   status: delegated\n221: \n222: - id: benchmark-synthesis\n223:   issue: gh:108\n224:   title: Combine the benchmark set and tooling spikes into the actual benchmark plan\n225:   kind: build\n226:   needs: [benchmark-set-spike, benchmark-tooling-spike]\n227:   prio: 3\n228:   status: delegated\n229: \n230: - id: record-argument-boundary\n231:   title: Oddity -- the paren-free record argument reaches across the definition boundary; settle it\n232:   kind: decide\n233:   needs: []\n234:   status: todo\n235: \n236: - id: jsonlines-statement-shape\n237:   title: Oddity -- jsonlines is a call-shaped statement; settle its shape\n238:   kind: decide\n239:   needs: []\n240:   status: todo\n241: \n242: - id: ternary-vs-match\n243:   title: Is the ternary redundant now that match covers it? Retire, keep, or demote\n244:   kind: decide\n245:   needs: []\n246:   prio: 2\n247:   status: todo\n248: \n249: - id: sum-max-reductions\n250:   title: sum and max as builtin reductions -- shape, element types, Opt on empty (euler-ergonomics row 1)\n251:   kind: decide\n252:   needs: []\n253:   prio: 2\n254:   status: todo\n255: \n256: - id: tail-call-contract\n257:   title: Self-tail-calls run in constant stack, as contract -- every backend (euler-ergonomics row 2)\n258:   kind: decide\n259:   needs: []\n260:   prio: 2\n261:   status: todo\n262: \n263: - id: first-search-cut\n264:   title: first as a value-layer search cut vs the draft's full story (euler-ergonomics row 5)\n265:   kind: decide\n266:   needs: []\n267:   status: todo\n268: \n269: - id: slices-decide\n270:   title: Slices as index specs -- clamp vs Opt at the boundary (euler-ergonomics row 6)\n271:   kind: decide\n272:   needs: []\n273:   status: todo\n274: \n275: - id: sort-by-max-by\n276:   title: sort_by and max_by -- ordering through a scalar projection (euler-ergonomics row 7)\n277:   kind: build\n278:   needs: [sum-max-reductions]\n279:   status: todo\n280: \n281: - id: param-destructuring\n282:   title: Record parameters destructure the way match arms already do -- spelling (euler-ergonomics row 8)\n283:   kind: decide\n284:   needs: []\n285:   status: todo\n286: \n287: - id: bi