"type":"file","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/plans/board.yaml","text":"# The task board (scheduler v2, maintainer-specified 2026-08-29): every unblocked task is by\n# definition ready to be picked up, and up to EIGHT build lanes run at once\n# (raised from five 2026-08-30; decide rows queue for the maintainer separately\n# and never consume a lane or a ready-set slot).\n#\n# Done rows do not live here (issue #113): landing a task MOVES its row to\n# plans/board-archive.yaml (same schema, append-only) instead of flipping status in place, so\n# this file stays the ~quarter of the board that is still live -- the loop's single most-read\n# file, and every tick pays for its length. A needs/soft id not found on this live board is\n# satisfied: it must have landed and been archived. Consult the archive only for provenance,\n# never to decide whether something is blocking.\n#\n# Fields: id (slug; gh:N when a GitHub issue carries the spec), title, kind, needs, soft,\n# prio, status.\n#   kind: build  = delegatable implementation work (enwiro-delegate out, land-delegated-work in)\n#         decide = needs a grilling/design session with the maintainer before anything builds\n#   needs: HARD blockers -- forced order; a task with an un-done need is not pickable at all.\n#          An id absent from this file is satisfied, not missing.\n#   soft:  SOFT blockers -- convenient order that saves effort or time (file-footprint\n#          overlaps, avoid-rework sequencing). A task with un-done soft blockers is still\n#          pickable, just ranked below less-soft-blocked work. Same absent-is-satisfied rule.\n#   prio:  1 (highest) .. 5; omitted means 3. Sorts WITHIN a soft-blockedness category, so\n#          soft order outweighs raw priority -- but among fully unblocked tasks, prio alone\n#          decides. Efficiency/process improvements are prio tasks by standing rule.\n#   status: todo | delegated  (done rows move to board-archive.yaml; \"blocked\" is derived from\n#           needs, never stored)\n#   lane:  which worker-pool lane a delegated row runs in (lane-1 .. lane-5, gh:124); the\n#          tick scripts resolve its worktree through the env symlink. Absent means the\n#          classic per-issue env (worktree issue-<N>). Set at dispatch, travels to the\n#          archive with the row.\n#   model: which model the delegated session runs -- omitted means sonnet (the default for\n#          regular build work); \"fable\" is reserved for design-heavy or cross-cutting builds\n#          the coordinator judges worth it; \"haiku\" is for mechanical work with an obvious\n#          done-state (renames, sweeps, small config/UI tweaks) where cheaper and faster\n#          beats smarter (maintainer rule, 2026-08-30). decide rows have no model; they are\n#          the human.\n#\n# Picking the ready set (drive skill executes this): drop hard-blocked rows (done rows are\n# already gone); group the rest by soft-blockedness (count of un-done soft blockers, in-flight\n# ones included); least soft-blocked category first, prio within each. TWO queues from that\n# ordering (2026-08-30): every ready decide goes to the maintainer's grill/mail queue, and the\n# top ready builds fill the free lanes up to the cap. List position is a tiebreak only. A\n# needs-cycle, or todo rows remaining with nothing pickable and nothing in flight, is a\n# deadlock and gets reported.\n- id: local-binding-design\n  issue: gh:87\n  title: Grill local bindings inside an expression -- the where/as shaped gap (emuto survey adopt)\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  status: todo\n\n- id: csv-inputs-idea\n  issue: gh:88\n  title: Grill the DSV source shape -- delimiter vs nullary sources (worker analysis, gh:88 comment)\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  prio: 4\n  status: todo\n\n- id: int64-wire-form\n  issue: gh:89\n  title: Decide the Int64 wire form -- input refuses it pending the codec call (gh:83 escalation)\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  prio: 3\n  status: todo\n\n- id: euler-slow-fragments-2\n  issue: gh:93\n  title: Batch 3's correct-but-slow problems, parked with the same tier question as gh:90\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  soft: [euler-slow-fragments]\n  prio: 3\n  status: todo\n\n- id: python-recursion-limit\n  issue: gh:132\n  title: Python backend never raises sys' default recursion limit -- breaks real-sized recursive programs (found via euler-11)\n  kind: build\n  needs: []\n  prio: 3\n  status: delegated\n\n- id: euler-pages-restore\n  issue: gh:133\n  title: Restore the Euler 8/11/13/18 docs pages now that tests/euler_real_data.rs verifies them (gh:129 follow-up)\n  kind: build\n  needs: []\n  soft: [python-recursion-limit]\n  prio: 3\n  status: delegated\n\n- id: projection-style-demotion\n  issue: gh:99\n  title: Demote map(.field) for pure projection -- style and sweep, not a refusal\n  kind: build\n  needs: []\n  prio: 3\n  soft: [concat-retirement]\n  status: delegated\n\n- id: euler-slow-fragments\n  issue: gh:90\n  title: Decide the slow-fragment tier -- Euler 10 and 14 solve correctly but cost minutes on the weak backends\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  prio: 3\n  status: todo\n\n- id: matcher-totality-and-alt-design\n  title: Grill matcher totality measurement, alt-composition (one arm, many patterns), and the parser-combinator stress test\n  kind: decide\n  needs: [auto-matchers-design]\n  prio: 1\n  status: todo\n\n- id: matcher-model-clarification\n  issue: gh:122\n  title: Grill the matching system's conceptual model -- base matcher kinds, how conditions enter, composition with type matchers (maintainer compose note)\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  soft: [matcher-totality-and-alt-design]\n  prio: 2\n  status: todo\n\n- id: variant-types-flip\n  title: Variants become capitalized types with lowercase constructors, per the auto-matchers ratification -- subtype rules planned first, then the migration (corpus, examples, README, and docs/guides+tutorial+reference)\n  kind: build\n  needs: [matcher-totality-and-alt-design]\n  prio: 2\n  model: fable\n  status: todo\n\n- id: shell-out-design\n  title: Grill the syntax for calling external CLI programs -- bash-convenient or better\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  status: todo\n\n- id: stdin-syntax-design\n  title: Grill the one-stdin-source syntax, once type flow makes parse steps possible\n  kind: decide\n  needs: [type-flow-rework]\n  status: todo\n\n- id: stdin-redesign-build\n  title: Retire the three stdin keywords for the one-source design\n  kind: build\n  needs: [stdin-syntax-design]\n  model: fable\n  status: todo\n\n- id: function-signature-ergonomics\n  title: Grill destructuring params and pipeline-first bodies -- wizard round with real code\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  status: todo\n\n- id: overloading-and-traits-design\n  title: Grill function overloading and Rust-style traits -- the direction that dissolves concat and kin\n  kind: decide\n  needs: [precedent-survey]\n  status: todo\n\n- id: mutation-semantics-design\n  title: Grill privileged/shared references -- mutation as a static optimization, no borrow checker\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  prio: 4\n  status: todo\n\n- id: void-functions-design\n  issue: gh:58\n  title: Grill void functions -- formalize functions that map to nothing but may have side effects (maintainer idea, streams tutorial annotation)\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  status: todo\n\n- id: range-stream-source-design\n  issue: gh:127\n  title: Grill whether range should become a Stream source -- Q1/Q13 amendment to ADR 0001 (prelude-inventory approved finding, gh:105/gh:121)\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  status: todo\n\n- id: q37-float-semantics\n  title: Grill Q37 -- float printing agreement, NaN/Infinity, division by zero\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  status: todo\n\n- id: benchmark-goals\n  title: Grill what workloads define the performance thesis, then plan the benchmark suite\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  prio: 4\n  status: todo\n\n- id: float-build\n  title: Implement Float (IEEE binary64 per ADR 0007) across the backends\n  kind: build\n  needs: [q37-float-semantics]\n  status: todo\n\n- id: lines-utf8-edge\n  issue: gh:102\n  title: Pin what a non-UTF-8 byte arriving via lines does, on every backend\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  status: todo\n\n- id: jq-printer-cycle-refusal\n  issue: gh:116\n  title: jq -- recursive-enum printers refuse a mutual cycle the way ordered() refuses one (issue-94 review)\n  kind: build\n  needs: []\n  prio: 3\n  soft: [concat-retirement]\n  status: delegated\n\n- id: benchmark-synthesis\n  issue: gh:108\n  title: Combine the benchmark set and tooling spikes into the actual benchmark plan\n  kind: build\n  needs: [benchmark-set-spike, benchmark-tooling-spike]\n  prio: 3\n  status: delegated\n\n- id: record-argument-boundary\n  title: Oddity -- the paren-free record argument reaches across the definition boundary; settle it\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  status: todo\n\n- id: jsonlines-statement-shape\n  title: Oddity -- jsonlines is a call-shaped statement; settle its shape\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  status: todo\n\n- id: ternary-vs-match\n  title: Is the ternary redundant now that match covers it? Retire, keep, or demote\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  prio: 2\n  status: todo\n\n- id: sum-max-reductions\n  title: sum and max as builtin reductions -- shape, element types, Opt on empty (euler-ergonomics row 1)\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  prio: 2\n  status: todo\n\n- id: tail-call-contract\n  title: Self-tail-calls run in constant stack, as contract -- every backend (euler-ergonomics row 2)\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  prio: 2\n  status: todo\n\n- id: first-search-cut\n  title: first as a value-layer search cut vs the draft's full story (euler-ergonomics row 5)\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  status: todo\n\n- id: slices-decide\n  title: Slices as index specs -- clamp vs Opt at the boundary (euler-ergonomics row 6)\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  status: todo\n\n- id: sort-by-max-by\n  title: sort_by and max_by -- ordering through a scalar projection (euler-ergonomics row 7)\n  kind: build\n  needs: [sum-max-reductions]\n  status: todo\n\n- id: param-destructuring\n  title: Record parameters destructure the way match arms already do -- spelling (euler-ergonomics row 8)\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  status: todo\n\n- id: bigint-tracking\n  issue: gh:112\n  title: Arbitrary-precision integers -- tracked, deliberately unscheduled\n  kind: build\n  needs: []\n  prio: 5\n  status: todo\n\n- id: js-node-web-split-design\n  issue: gh:118\n  title: Grill the JS Node/Web target split, optional TS type generation, the web-incompatible-builtin escape hatch, and a compiler config file (maintainer compose note)\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  status: todo\n\n- id: method-call-syntax-design\n  issue: gh:119\n  title: Grill method-like call syntax -- functions that target a type with extra params (maintainer compose note)\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  status: todo\n\n- id: benchmark-spike-citations\n  issue: gh:125\n  title: Cite TechEmpower/SPEC license claims in benchmark-suite-spike.md (gh:106 review follow-up)\n  kind: build\n  model: haiku\n  needs: []\n  prio: 4\n  status: delegated\n\n- id: emit-rs-concat-helper\n  issue: gh:126\n  title: Extract emit_rs.rs's Concat dispatch arm into a named helper, matching sibling backends (gh:97 review follow-up)\n  kind: build\n  model: haiku\n  needs: []\n  prio: 4\n  status: delegated\n\n- id: draft-intro-migration\n  issue: gh:134\n  title: Migrate draft.md's identity sections (what this is, principles, values, worked programs, non-goals) to a docs overview page, then delete them\n  kind: build\n  needs: []\n  soft: [draft-questions-home]\n  prio: 4\n  status: delegated\n\n- id: draft-core-model-migration\n  title: Migrate the two-layer/cardinality core model to a concepts guide; embedded open threads go to the tracker (draft-split)\n  kind: build\n  model: fable\n  needs: []\n  soft: [draft-int