n (draft-split)\n  kind: build\n  needs: []\n  soft: [draft-intro-migration, draft-questions-home]\n  prio: 4\n  status: todo\n\n- id: draft-str-adr\n  title: Record the Str contract as an ADR per the string spike's recommendation, then delete the draft's strings section (draft-split)\n  kind: build\n  needs: []\n  soft: [draft-intro-migration, lines-utf8-edge]\n  prio: 3\n  status: todo\n\n- id: draft-mutation-migration\n  title: Record the mutation decisions once they land and delete both mutation sections (draft-split)\n  kind: build\n  needs: [mutation-semantics-design, binary-op-multiplicity-design]\n  prio: 4\n  status: todo\n\n- id: binary-op-multiplicity-design\n  title: Grill binary operators over multi-valued operands (cartesian, zip, or explicit) and the record-forming update's spelling -- Q2/Q3 (draft-split)\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  prio: 3\n  status: todo\n\n- id: search-and-fold-design\n  title: Grill the search vocabulary (choice, cut, .., ordering) and the applicative fold block -- unratified draft sections (draft-split)\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  soft: [first-search-cut]\n  prio: 4\n  status: todo\n\n- id: offload-boundary-design\n  title: Grill the offload/vectorization thesis -- kernel admissibility, batch invariance, parallel basis, tensors (draft-split)\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  soft: [benchmark-goals]\n  prio: 5\n  status: todo\n\n- id: draft-md-cleanup-review\n  title: Review what remains of draft.md after every split row lands; assign or delete the remainder, retire the file (draft-split)\n  kind: build\n  needs: [draft-questions-home, draft-intro-migration, draft-core-model-migration, draft-access-model-migration, draft-numbers-operators-migration, draft-records-migration, draft-streams-migration, draft-calls-modules-migration, draft-matching-migration, draft-prototype-findings-migration, draft-str-adr, draft-mutation-migration, binary-op-multiplicity-design, search-and-fold-design, offload-boundary-design]\n  prio: 4\n  status: todo","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":444,"totalLines":444,"truncated":false}},"title":"plans/board.yaml","time":{"start":1788129519804,"end":1788129519816}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The task: build a streaming pipe-to-subprocess primitive (`pipe_through`). This is a significant feature. The issue says Q35 should \"land, or at least have a concrete enough shape, before this is implementable.\" The issue is OPEN and there are 0 comments. The brief says \"read every comment before touching anything\" - there are no comments.\n\nThe issue says the Q35 dependency should land first. But my task brief says \"Depends on Q35's stdout/stderr effect model -- check draft.md and the ADRs for that model before designing the primitive's signature.\"\n\nLet me look at the board.yaml to understand where this sits in the drive plan, and check if there's a design doc for pipe_through already. Let me also look at the shell-out-design board row.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_054d3246a001B6WoBWVUiV2o5D","sessionID":"ses_fab2d85e2ffebDq1A7tlFaR4vv","messageID":"msg_054d3044d001em93yjQTQOTdu0"}}
