{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788129699333,"sessionID":"ses_fab2d85e2ffebDq1A7tlFaR4vv","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-84f0d28877b5325e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"ls docs/reference/syntax docs/reference/builtins docs/reference/operators"},"output":"docs/reference/builtins:\nchars.md\ncollect.md\nfields.md\nflatten.md\ni64.md\njsonlines.md\nlength.md\nmap.md\nmax.md\nrange.md\nreverse.md\nselect.md\nsort.md\nstr.md\nsum.md\ntail.md\n\ndocs/reference/operators:\narithmetic.md\nboolean.md\ncomparison.md\nconditional.md\nmatch.md\npipe.md\nprojection.md\nspecs.md\nunwrap.md\n\ndocs/reference/syntax:\nfunctions.md\nprograms.md\n","metadata":{"output":"docs/reference/builtins:\nchars.md\ncollect.md\nfields.md\nflatten.md\ni64.md\njsonlines.md\nlength.md\nmap.md\nmax.md\nrange.md\nreverse.md\nselect.md\nsort.md\nstr.md\nsum.md\ntail.md\n\ndocs/reference/operators:\narithmetic.md\nboolean.md\ncomparison.md\nconditional.md\nmatch.md\npipe.md\nprojection.md\nspecs.md\nunwrap.md\n\ndocs/reference/syntax:\nfunctions.md\nprograms.md\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"ls docs/reference/syntax docs/reference/builtins docs/reference/operators","time":{"start":1788129699331,"end":1788129699333}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"So bare application is right-recursive: `f g x` is `f(g(x))`. And `f(x)` is parenthesized. Multi-arg calls like `pipe_through(\"grep\", [\"foo\"])` with a comma... Let me check if the parser supports comma-separated argument lists. Let me search the parser.\n\nActually `pipe_through(\"grep\", [\"foo\"])` in the issue is written with a comma. Does toylang support that? Let me look at the parse.rs and the syntax reference. Let me grep for comma in parse.rs and in docs/reference/syntax.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_054d5e40d001gpRQiXFYLuFN4x","sessionID":"ses_fab2d85e2ffebDq1A7tlFaR4vv","messageID":"msg_054d5b772001pAGf3PwktalSPq"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788129699960,"sessionID":"ses_fab2d85e2ffebDq1A7tlFaR4vv","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-b7818fc974612266","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/docs/reference/syntax/programs.md"},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/docs/reference/syntax/programs.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # A program\n2: \n3: A program is declarations followed by one expression, and the expression's value is what\n4: prints. There are no statements, no `main`, and no print call: output needs no side effect,\n5: because the program is the expression.\n6: \n7: ```toylang\n8: # Comments start with `#` and run to the end of the line.\n9: type Pair = {a: Int, b: Int}\n10: \n11: fn total(p: Pair) -> Int = p.a + p.b\n12: \n13: {sum: total({a: 1, b: 2})}\n14: ```\n15: \n16: ```output\n17: {\"sum\":3}\n18: ```\n19: \n20: The declarations are [type aliases](../types/alias.md), [enums](../types/enum.md), and\n21: [functions](functions.md), in any order; a function may call one defined later. `pub` on a\n22: `fn` marks it for a future module story and currently changes nothing in a program's own\n23: file.\n24: \n25: How the value prints: a top-level `Str` prints raw; everything else prints as compact JSON,\n26: with record fields in the order their type declares them. A program whose outermost\n27: expression is the\n28: [`jsonlines`](../builtins/jsonlines.md) sink prints line by line instead and has no value.\n29: \n30: Name casing is a rule, not a convention: a capitalized name is a type, a lowercase name is\n31: a value. Field and variant names come from data and are exempt.\n32: \n33: Everything is checked before anything runs: types, match coverage, stream linearity, the\n34: 32-bit literal rule. What remains at runtime is the arithmetic refusals (`/ 0`, `% 0`),\n35: absent-value unwraps, and input that misses its declared type.\n\n(End of file - total 35 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# A program\n\nA program is declarations followed by one expression, and the expression's value is what\nprints. There are no statements, no `main`, and no print call: output needs no side effect,\nbecause the program is the expression.\n\n```toylang\n# Comments start with `#` and run to the end of the line.\ntype Pair = {a: Int, b: Int}\n\nfn total(p: Pair) -> Int = p.a + p.b\n\n{sum: total({a: 1, b: 2})}\n```\n\n```output\n{\"sum\":3}\n```\n\nThe declarations are [type aliases](../types/alias.md), [enums](../types/enum.md), and","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/docs/reference/syntax/programs.md","text":"# A program\n\nA program is declarations followed by one expression, and the expression's value is what\nprints. There are no statements, no `main`, and no print call: output needs no side effect,\nbecause the program is the expression.\n\n```toylang\n# Comments start with `#` and run to the end of the line.\ntype Pair = {a: Int, b: Int}\n\nfn total(p: Pair) -> Int = p.a + p.b\n\n{sum: total({a: 1, b: 2})}\n```\n\n```output\n{\"sum\":3}\n```\n\nThe declarations are [type aliases](../types/alias.md), [enums](../types/enum.md), and\n[functions](functions.md), in any order; a function may call one defined later. `pub` on a\n`fn` marks it for a future module story and currently changes nothing in a program's own\nfile.\n\nHow the value prints: a top-level `Str` prints raw; everything else prints as compact JSON,\nwith record fields in the order their type declares them. A program whose outermost\nexpression is the\n[`jsonlines`](../builtins/jsonlines.md) sink prints line by line instead and has no value.\n\nName casing is a rule, not a convention: a capitalized name is a type, a lowercase name is\na value. Field and variant names come from data and are exempt.\n\nEverything is checked before anything runs: types, match coverage, stream linearity, the\n32-bit literal rule. What remains at runtime is the arithmetic refusals (`/ 0`, `% 0`),\nabsent-value unwraps, and input that misses its declared type.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":35,"totalLines":35,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/reference/syntax/programs.md","time":{"start":1788129699940,"end":1788129699959}},"id":"prt_054d5e600001RfyMhWTMsbOR3M","sessionID":"ses_fab2d85e2ffebDq1A7tlFaR4vv","messageID":"msg_054d5b772001pAGf3PwktalSPq"}}
