{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788130264686,"sessionID":"ses_fab2d85e2ffebDq1A7tlFaR4vv","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-965ae3f59880d671","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/tests/docs.rs","pattern":"BUILTIN|builtin|reference/builtins|jsonlines"},"output":"Found 100 matches (more matches available)\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/tests/unwrap.rs:\n  Line 19: /// `str` is a builtin, so a program cannot define its own and silently mean something else.\n\n  Line 21: fn a_builtin_cannot_be_redefined() {\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/tests/type_flow.rs:\n  Line 168: fn a_polymorphic_builtin_still_synthesises_its_argument() {\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/tests/docs.rs:\n  Line 177: /// The reference is complete for everything implemented, checkably: a builtin without a page\n\n  Line 180: fn every_builtin_has_a_reference_page() {\n\n  Line 181:     let missing: Vec<&str> = toylang::check::BUILTIN_NAMES\n\n  Line 185:                 .join(\"reference/builtins\")\n\n  Line 192:         \"builtins without a reference page under docs/reference/builtins/: {}\",\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/tests/bare_application.rs:\n  Line 72: /// name inside `Call`, and so are reserved the same way every other builtin is.\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/tests/char.rs:\n  Line 44: fn jsonlines_cannot_print_a_char() {\n\n  Line 45:     insta::assert_snapshot!(err(\"jsonlines(chars(\\\"a\\\"))\"));\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/tests/aliases.rs:\n  Line 92: fn a_builtin_type_cannot_be_redefined() {\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/tests/streaming.rs:\n  Line 18: jsonlines(adults(inputs))\n\n  Line 32: jsonlines(names(keep(inputs)))\n\n  Line 35: /// A `lines`-sourced pipeline ending in `jsonlines`: a shape the old recognizer never knew\n\n  Line 41: jsonlines(shout(lines))\n\n  Line 251: /// shape on all seven is `jsonlines_of_lines.yaml`'s job.\n\n  Line 275: jsonlines(render(inputs))\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/tests/generics.rs:\n  Line 34: fn a_builtin_scalar_takes_no_argument() {\n\n  Line 56: fn a_type_parameter_cannot_take_a_builtin_name() {\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/tests/reductions.rs:\n  Line 48: /// A builtin is a reserved name: a program that defines `sum` and means something else by it\n\n  Line 51: fn a_builtin_cannot_be_redefined() {\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/tests/jsonlines.rs:\n  Line 1: //! `jsonlines`, the sink: legal only as the program's outermost expression, taking a `Vec<T>`\n\n  Line 14: /// Polymorphic, so it is not in the fixed builtin table `fn`-redefinition normally checks\n\n  Line 15: /// against; it needs its own guard for the same reason every other builtin has one.\n\n  Line 17: fn jsonlines_cannot_be_redefined() {\n\n  Line 18:     insta::assert_snapshot!(err(\"fn jsonlines(x: Int) -> Int = x\\n\\njsonlines(1)\"));\n\n  Line 22: fn jsonlines_needs_a_vec() {\n\n  Line 23:     insta::assert_snapshot!(err(r#\"jsonlines(\"not a vec\")\"#));\n\n  Line 26: /// A sink has no result type, so there is nowhere a nested `jsonlines` could put one: it is\n\n  Line 29: fn jsonlines_cannot_be_nested() {\n\n  Line 30:     insta::assert_snapshot!(err(\"jsonlines([jsonlines([1])])\"));\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/tests/int64.rs:\n  Line 127:             \"fn f(s: Stream<{ts: Int64}>) -> Stream<{ts: Int64}> = s\\n\\njsonlines(f(inputs))\"\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/tests/corpus/arith_mul.yaml:\n  Line 7: node_types: [arith.mul, builtin.str, int]\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/tests/corpus/arith_add.yaml:\n  Line 7: node_types: [arith.add, builtin.str, int]\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/tests/corpus/arith_div_trunc.yaml:\n  Line 7: node_types: [arith.div, builtin.str, int]\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/tests/corpus/arith_sub.yaml:\n  Line 7: node_types: [arith.sub, builtin.str, int]\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/tests/corpus/arith_rem_sign.yaml:\n  Line 7: node_types: [arith.rem, builtin.str, concat, int, str]\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/tests/corpus/chars_unicode_honest.yaml:\n  Line 13: node_types: [builtin.chars, builtin.length, str]\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/tests/corpus/arith_precedence.yaml:\n  Line 7: node_types: [arith.add, arith.mul, builtin.str, concat, int, str]\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/tests/corpus/cond_chain.yaml:\n  Line 7: node_types: [builtin.str, compare.eq, conditional, int]\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/tests/corpus/char_range_and_complement.yaml:\n  Line 18: node_types: [application, builtin.chars, builtin.length, compare.ge, compare.le, int, local, logic.and, logic.not, pipe, record-literal, selection.collapse, selection.narrow, str, unwrap, var]\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/tests/corpus/arith_neg.yaml:\n  Line 7: node_types: [arith.sub, builtin.str, concat, int, str]\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/tests/corpus/enum_inputs.yaml:\n  Line 11:   jsonlines render inputs\n\n  Line 23: node_types: [application, builtin.jsonlines, inputs, local, map-over, match, pipe, projection, str, var]\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/tests/corpus/div_by_zero.yaml:\n  Line 7: node_types: [arith.div, builtin.str, int]\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/tests/corpus/enum_inputs_reject.yaml:\n  Line 9:   jsonlines render inputs\n\n  Line 17: node_types: [application, builtin.jsonlines, inputs, local, map-over, match, pipe, projection, str, var]\n\n\n/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/iss