o\", \"cy\"])\n\n\n(Results truncated. Consider using a more specific path or pattern.)","metadata":{"matches":100,"truncated":true},"title":"BUILTIN|builtin|reference/builtins|jsonlines","time":{"start":1788130264657,"end":1788130264684}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now I understand the streaming liveness probe pattern. Let me now make the design decisions and settle the plan. Let me check tests/docs.rs to understand the docs requirement for builtins (every builtin needs a reference page), and look at tags.rs builtin_tag, and the jsonlines.md reference page.\n\nLet me also check the docs harness requirement for builtins pages.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_054de8434001HDwde48ZL5cRMZ","sessionID":"ses_fab2d85e2ffebDq1A7tlFaR4vv","messageID":"msg_054de7aac001Ew3RtXxn49CWh3"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788130265291,"sessionID":"ses_fab2d85e2ffebDq1A7tlFaR4vv","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-b87622d9760949ad","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/src/tags.rs"},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/src/tags.rs</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: //! Human-readable tags for the AST shapes a program exercises.\n2: //!\n3: //! Drawn from `tir::Kind`, not `ast::Expr`: `select`, `map`, and even `+` only resolve into\n4: //! their real meaning once type checking has run (`ast::Expr::Call` covers a user function, a\n5: //! builtin, and `select`/`map` alike, and `+` covers both `Concat` and `Arith::Add`). Every\n6: //! corpus case compiles, so `Tir` is always available.\n7: //!\n8: //! Where CONTEXT.md already names a concept, the tag uses that name -- `application` for a call,\n9: //! `projection` for a field access, `selection` for both `select(...)` and an index, since the\n10: //! glossary treats those as the same idea under different specs. `map-over` is the one deliberate\n11: //! departure: CONTEXT.md reserves `Map` for the not-yet-built dict-like type, so the `map(f)`\n12: //! builtin gets a different word rather than colliding with it.\n13: \n14: use std::collections::BTreeSet;\n15: \n16: use crate::ast::BinOp;\n17: use crate::tir::{Builtin, Kind, Program, Tir};\n18: \n19: /// Every tag exercised by `program`, sorted and deduplicated. A tag with no sub-case is its bare\n20: /// name (`projection`); one with a sub-case is `parent.child` (`arith.add`, `builtin.range`).\n21: pub fn node_types(program: &Program) -> Vec<String> {\n22:     let mut tags = BTreeSet::new();\n23:     for func in &program.funcs {\n24:         walk(&func.body, &mut tags);\n25:     }\n26:     walk(&program.body, &mut tags);\n27:     tags.into_iter().collect()\n28: }\n29: \n30: fn walk(tir: &Tir, tags: &mut BTreeSet<String>) {\n31:     tags.insert(tag(tir));\n32:     match &tir.kind {\n33:         Kind::Str(_)\n34:         | Kind::Int(_)\n35:         | Kind::Var(_)\n36:         | Kind::Local(_)\n37:         | Kind::Input\n38:         | Kind::Inputs\n39:         | Kind::Lines => {}\n40:         Kind::VecLit(items) => items.iter().for_each(|i| walk(i, tags)),\n41:         Kind::RecordLit { fields } => fields.iter().for_each(|(_, v)| walk(v, tags)),\n42:         Kind::EnumLit { payload, .. } => {\n43:             if let Some(p) = payload {\n44:                 walk(p, tags);\n45:             }\n46:         }\n47:         Kind::Call { arg, .. } => {\n48:             if let Some(a) = arg {\n49:                 walk(a, tags);\n50:             }\n51:         }\n52:         Kind::Concat(lhs, rhs) => {\n53:             walk(lhs, tags);\n54:             walk(rhs, tags);\n55:         }\n56:         Kind::Arith { lhs, rhs, .. }\n57:         | Kind::Compare { lhs, rhs, .. }\n58:         | Kind::Logic { lhs, rhs, .. } => {\n59:             walk(lhs, tags);\n60:             walk(rhs, tags);\n61:         }\n62:         Kind::Cond {\n63:             cond,\n64:             then,\n65:             otherwise,\n66:         } => {\n67:             walk(cond, tags);\n68:             walk(then, tags);\n69:             walk(otherwise, tags);\n70:         }\n71:         Kind::Bind { value, body, .. }\n72:         | Kind::Map {\n73:             source: value,\n74:             body,\n75:             ..\n76:         }\n77:         | Kind::OptMap {\n78:             source: value,\n79:             body,\n80:             ..\n81:         } => {\n82:             walk(value, tags);\n83:             walk(body, tags);\n84:         }\n85:         Kind::Select { source, pred, .. } => {\n86:             walk(source, tags);\n87:             walk(pred, tags);\n88:         }\n89:         Kind::Field { base, .. } | Kind::Unwrap { base } | Kind::Not(base) => walk(base, tags),\n90:         Kind::Builtin { arg, .. } => walk(arg, tags),\n91:         Kind::Index { base, index, .. } => {\n92:             walk(base, tags);\n93:             walk(index, tags);\n94:         }\n95:         Kind::Match { subject, arms, .. } => {\n96:             walk(subject, tags);\n97:             for a in arms {\n98:                 if let Some(g) = &a.guard {\n99:                     walk(g, tags);\n100:                 }\n101:                 walk(&a.body, tags);\n102:             }\n103:         }\n104:     }\n105: }\n106: \n107: fn tag(tir: &Tir) -> String {\n108:     match &tir.kind {\n109:         Kind::Str(_) => \"str\".into(),\n110:         // One literal kind, two widths: which one this literal has is the node's type's to\n111:         // say (kantord/toylang#83), so the tag reads it rather than the kind.\n112:         Kind::Int(_) if tir.ty == crate::ty::Type::Int64 => \"int64\".into(),\n113:         Kind::Int(_) => \"int\".into(),\n114:         Kind::VecLit(_) => \"vec-literal\".into(),\n115:         Kind::RecordLit { .. } => \"record-literal\".into(),\n116:         // CONTEXT.md's terms: a `variant` is one alternative, a `unit variant` carries nothing.\n117:         Kind::EnumLit { payload: None, .. } => \"variant.unit\".into(),\n118:         Kind::EnumLit {\n119:             payload: Some(_), ..\n120:         } => \"variant.payload\".into(),\n121:         Kind::Var(_) => \"var\".into(),\n122:         Kind::Local(_) => \"local\".into(),\n123:         Kind::Input => \"input\".into(),\n124:         Kind::Lines => \"lines\".into(),\n125:         Kind::Call { .. } => \"application\".into(),\n126:         Kind::Concat(..) => \"concat\".into(),\n127:         Kind::Arith { op, .. } => format!(\"arith.{}\", binop_tag(*op)),\n128:         Kind::Cond { .. } => \"conditional\".into(),\n129:         Kind::Compare { op, .. } => format!(\"compare.{}\", binop_tag(*op)),\n130:         Kind::Logic { op, .. } => format!(\"logic.{op}\"),\n131:         Kind::Not(_) => \"logic.not\".into(),\n132:         Kind::Bind { .. } => \"pipe\".into(),\n133:         Kind::Map { .. } => \"map-over\".into(),\n134:         Kind::OptMap { .. } => \"opt-map\".into(),\n135:         Kind::Select { .. } => \"selection.narrow\".into(),\n136:         Kind::Field { .. } => \"projection\".into(),\n137:         Kind::Builtin { which, .. } => format!(\"builtin.{}\", builtin_tag(*which)),\n138:         Kind::Unwrap { .. } => \"unwrap\".into(),\n139:         Kind::Index { .. } => \"selection.collapse\".into(),\n140:         Kind::Inputs => \"inputs\".into(),\n141:         Kind::Match { .. } => \"match\".into(),\n142:     }\n143: }\n144: \n145: fn binop_tag(op: BinOp) -> &'static str {\n146:     match op {\n147:         BinOp::Add => \"add\",\n148:         BinOp::Sub => \"sub\",\n149:         BinOp::Mul => \"mul\",\n150:         BinOp::Div => \"div\",\n151:         BinOp::Rem => \"rem\",\n152:         BinOp::Eq => \"eq\",\n153:         BinOp::Ne => \"ne\",\n154:         BinOp::Lt => \"lt\",\n155:         BinOp::Le => \"le\",\n156:         BinOp::Gt => \"gt\",\n157:         BinOp::Ge => \"ge\",\n158:     }\n159: }\n160: \n161: fn builtin_tag(which: Builtin) -> &'static str {\n162:     match which {\n163:         Builtin::IntToStr => \"str\",\n164:         Builtin::IntToI64 => \"i64\",\n165:         Builtin::Range => \"range\",\n166:         Builtin::Collect => \"collect\",\n167:         Builtin::JsonLines => \"jsonlines\",\n168:         Builtin::Length => \"length\",\n169:         Builtin::Flatten => \"flatten\",\n170:         Builtin::Tail => \"tail\",\n171:         Builtin::Fields => \"fields\",\n172:         Builtin::Chars => \"chars\",\n173:         Builtin::Sort => \"sort\",\n174:         Builtin::Reverse => \"reverse\",\n175:         Builtin::Sum => \"sum\",\n176:         Builtin::Max => \"max\",\n177:     }\n178: }\n\n(End of file - total 178 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"//! Human-readable tags for the AST shapes a program exercises.\n//!\n//! Drawn from `tir::Kind`, not `ast::Expr`: `select`, `map`, and even `+` only resolve into\n//! their real meaning once type checking has run (`ast::Expr::Call` covers a user function, a\n//! builtin, and `select`/`map` alike, and `+` covers both `Concat` and `Arith::Add`). Every\n//! corpus case compiles, so `Tir` is always available.\n//!\n//! Where CONTEXT.md already names a concept, the tag uses that name -- `application` for a call,\n//! `projection` for a field access, `selection` for both `select(...)` and an index, since the\n//! glossary treats those as the same idea under different specs. `map-over` is the one deliberate\n//! departure: CONTEXT.md reserves `Map` for the not-yet-built dict-like type, so the `map(f)`\n//! builtin gets a different word rather than colliding with it.\n\nuse std::collections::BTreeSet;\n\nuse crate::ast::BinOp;\nuse crate::tir::{Builtin, Kind, Program, Tir};\n\n/// Every tag exercised by `program`, sorted and deduplicated. A tag with no sub-case is its bare\n/// name (`projection`); one with a sub-case is `parent.child` (`arith.add`, `builtin.range`).","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-158/src/tags.rs","text":"//! Human-readable tags for the AST shapes a program exercises.\n//!\n//! Drawn from `tir::Kind`, not `ast::Expr`: `select`, `map`, and even `+` only resolve into\n//! their real meaning once type checking has run (`ast::Expr::Call` covers a user function, a\n//! builtin, and `select`/`map` alike, and `+` covers both `Concat` and `Arith::Add`). Every\n//! corpus case compiles, so `Tir` is always available.\n//!\n//! Where CONTEXT.md already names a concept, the tag uses that name -- `application` for a call,\n//! `projection` for a field access, `selection` for both `select(...)` and an index, since the\n//! glossary treats those as the same idea under different specs. `map-over` is the one deliberate\n//! departure: CONTEXT.md reserves `Map` for the not-yet-built dict-like type, so the `map(f)`\n//! builtin gets a different word rather than colliding with it.\n\nuse std::collections::BTreeSet;\n\nuse crate::ast::BinOp;\nuse crate::tir::{Builtin, Kind, Program, Tir};\n\n/// Every tag exercised by `program`, sorted and deduplicated. A tag with no sub-case is its bare\n/// name (`projection`); one with a sub-case is `parent.child` (`arith.add`, `builtin.range`).\npub fn node_types(program: &Program) -> Vec<String> {\n    let mut tags = BTreeSet::new();\n    for func in &program.funcs {\n        walk(&func.body, &mut tags);\n    }\n    walk(&program.body, &mut tags);\n    tags.into_iter().collect()\n}\n\nfn walk(tir: &Tir, tags: &mut BTreeSet<String>) {\n    tags.insert(tag(tir));\n    match &tir.kind {\n        Kind::Str(_)\n        | Kind::Int(_)\n        | Kind::Var(_)\n        | Kind::Local(_)\n        | Kind::Input\n        | Kind::Inputs\n        | Kind::Lines => {}\n        Kind::VecLit(items) => items.iter().for_each(|i| walk(i, tags)),\n        Kind::RecordLit { fields } => fields.iter().for_each(|(_, v)| walk(v, tags)),\n        Kind::EnumLit { payload, .. } => {\n            if let Some(p) = payload {\n                walk(p, tags);\n            }\n        }\n        Kind::Call { arg, .. } => {\n            if let Some(a) = arg {\n                walk(a, tags);\n            }\n        }\n        Kind::Concat(lhs, rhs) => {\n            walk(lhs, tags);\n            walk(rhs, tags);\n        }\n        Kind::Arith { lhs, rhs, .. }\n        | Kind::Compare { lhs, rhs, .. }\n        | Kind::Logic { lhs, rhs, .. } => {\n            walk(lhs, tags);\n            walk(rhs, tags);\n        }\n        Kind::Cond {\n            cond,\n            then,\n            otherwise,\n        } => {\n            walk(cond, tags);\n            walk(then, tags);\n            walk(otherwise, tags);\n        }\n        Kind::Bind { value, body, .. }\n        | Kind::Map {\n            source: value,\n            body,\n            ..\n        }\n        | Kind::OptMap {\n            source: value,\n            body,\n            ..\n        } => {\n            walk(value, tags);\n            walk(body, tags);\n        }\n        Kind::Select { source, pred, .. } => {\n            walk(source, tags);\n            walk(pred, tags);\n        }\n        Kind::Field { base, .. } | Kind::Unwrap { base } | Kind::Not(base) => walk(base, tags),\n        Kind::Builtin { arg, .. } => walk(arg, tags),\n        Kind::Index { base, index, .. } => {\n            walk(base, tags);\n            walk(index, tags);\n        }\n        Kind::Match { subject, arms, .. } => {\n            walk(subject, tags);\n            for a in arms {\n                if let Some(g) = &a.guard {\n                    walk(g, tags);\n                }\n                walk(&a.body, tags);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nfn tag(tir: &Tir) -> String {\n    match &tir.kind {\n        Kind::Str(_) => \"str\".into(),\n        // One literal kind, two widths: which one this literal has is the node's type's to\n        // say (kantord/toylang#83), so the tag reads it rather than the kind.\n        Kind::Int(_) if tir.ty == crate::ty::Type::Int64 => \"int64\".into(),\n        Kind::Int(_) => \"int\".into(),\n        Kind::VecLit(_) => \"vec-literal\".into(),\n        Kind::RecordLit { .. } => \"record-literal\".into(),\n        // CONTEXT.md's terms: a `variant` is one alternative, a `unit variant` carries nothing.\n        Kind::EnumLit { payload: None, .. } => \"variant.unit\".into(),\n        Kind::EnumLit {\n            payload: Some(_), ..\n        } => \"variant.payload\".into(),\n        Kind::Var(_) => \"var\".into(),\n        Kind::Local(_) => \"local\".into(),\n        Kind::Input => \"input\".into(),\n        Kind::Lines => \"lines\".into(),\n        Kind::Call { .. } => \"application\".into(),\n        Kind::Concat(..) => \"concat\".into(),\n        Kind::Arith { op, .. } => format!(\"arith.{}\", binop_tag(*op)),\n        Kind::Cond { .. } => \"conditional\".into(),\n        Kind::Compare { op, .. } => format!(\"compare.{}\", binop_tag(*op)),\n        Kind::Logic { op, .. } => format!(\"logic.{op}\"),\n        Kind::Not(_) => \"logic.not\".into(),\n        Kind::Bind { .. } => \"pipe\".into(),\n        Kind::Map { .. } => \"map-over\".into(),\n        Kind::OptMap { .. } => \"opt-map\".into(),\n        Kind::Select { .. } => \"selection.narrow\".into(),\n        Kind::Field { .. } => \"projection\".into(),\n        Kind::Builtin { which, .. } => format!(\"builtin.{}\", builtin_tag(*which)),\n        Kind::Unwrap { .. } => \"unwrap\".into(),\n        Kind::Index { .. } => \"selection.collapse\".into(),\n        Kind::Inputs => \"inputs\".into(),\n        Kind::Match { .. } => \"match\".into(),\n    }\n}\n\nfn binop_tag(op: BinOp) -> &'static str {\n    match op {\n        BinOp::Add => \"add\",\n        BinOp::Sub => \"sub\",\n        BinOp::Mul => \"mul\",\n        BinOp::Div => \"div\",\n        BinOp::Rem => \"rem\",\n        BinOp::Eq => \"eq\",\n        BinOp::Ne => \"ne\",\n        BinOp::Lt => \"lt\",\n        BinOp::Le => \"le\",\n        BinOp::Gt => \"gt\",\n        BinOp::Ge => \"ge\",\n    }\n}\n\nfn builtin_tag(which: Builtin) -> &'static str {\n    match which {\n        Builtin::IntToStr => \"str\",\n        Builtin::IntToI64 => \"i64\",\n        Builtin::Range => \"range\",\n        Builtin::Collect => \"collect\",\n        Builtin::JsonLines => \"jsonlines\",\n        Builtin::Length => \"length\",\n        Builtin::Flatten => \"flatten\",\n        Builtin::Tail => \"tail\",\n        Builtin::Fields => \"fields\",\n        Builtin::Chars => \"chars\",\n        Builtin::Sort => \"sort\",\n        Builtin::Reverse => \"reverse\",\n        Builtin::Sum => \"sum\",\n        Builtin::Max => \"max\",\n    }\n}","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":178,"totalLines":178,"truncated":false}},"title":"src/tags.rs","time":{"start":1788130265278,"end":1788130265288}},"id":"prt_054de8656001SVfNGvQ3mcG3h7","sessionID":"ses_fab2d85e2ffebDq1A7tlFaR4vv","messageID":"msg_054de7aac001Ew3RtXxn49CWh3"}}
